entry.summary:
Your app's navigation is only as fast as your Link component. The default one just... navigates. I wanted more, so I built rockzy-link. Smart prefetching — analyzes and preloads routes users are likely to visit next, instead of prefetching everything and wasting bandwidth Route caching — back/forward navigation feels instant Scroll restoration — users land where they expect Offline hooks — hooks so your UI degrades gracefully when the network drops Navigation snapshots — capture and restore navigation state Accessibility — proper semantics out of the box npm i rockzy-link
import { Link } from 'rockzy-link';
// Drop-in replacement — prefetching just works <Link href="/dashboard" prefetch>Dashboard</Link>
I'm a developer from Liberia working mostly in Zig and JavaScript. I kept hitting the same wall: client-side navigation that felt sluggish no matter how optimized the pages were. The bottleneck was the Link itself. So I fixed it at the source. It's MIT licensed and I'd genuinely love feedback — try it, break it, tell me what's missing. npm: https://www.npmjs.com/package/rockzy-link https://github.com/psrockstar098/rockzy-link
